'''Polis Massa''' was a [[planetoid]] in a dense [[asteroid field]] located in the [[Subterrel sector]] of [[the galaxy]]'s [[Outer Rim Territories]], far from any major [[Hyperspace route|hyperspace lanes]]. At some point, Polis Massa was a [[planet]] located within the [[Star system|system]] of [[Polis Massa system|the same name]].<ref name="Ultimate Star Wars" /> The planet was home to a subterranean people called the [[Eellayin]] until it was [[Polis Massa cataclysm|destroyed]].<ref name="SWCL" /> But the rocky fragments of the planet still held relics of the Eelayin, which were collected and studied by [[Kallidahin]] [[archaeologist]]s.<ref name="SWCL" />

==History==
In [[519 BBY]] the [[Archaeological Research Council]] of [[Kallidah]] established a [[Polis Massa Base|base]] on one of the largest [[asteroid]]s in order to excavate throughout the asteroid belt to study the reasons behind [[Polis Massa cataclysm|the planet's destruction]]. Remnants of the Eellayin, their ancestors, were scant. However in [[69 BBY]], researchers found the ruins of the underground city of [[Wiyentaah]]. Since then, the Local Dig was set up and was progressively excavated.<ref name="SWCL" /> The [[Kallidahin]] eventually came to be known as Polis Massans due to their extensive time on the planetoid.<ref name="CE" />

Following the execution of [[Order 66]], Polis Massa became a haven for surviving [[Jedi]].<ref name="Ultimate Star Wars" /> Shortly after the [[lightsaber]] [[Duel on Mustafar|duel]] between [[Obi-Wan Kenobi]] and [[Anakin Skywalker|Darth Vader]] on [[Mustafar]], [[Senator]] [[Padmé Amidala Naberrie|Padmé Amidala]] gave birth to twins, [[Luke Skywalker|Luke]] and [[Leia Skywalker Organa Solo|Leia]], at the [[Polis Massa medical facility|medical facility]] located on Polis Massa. [[Yoda]] contacted the [[Death|deceased]] [[Jedi Master]] [[Qui-Gon Jinn]] at the same time, and Jinn told Yoda that he would teach him how to [[Force spirit|retain consciousness]] after death. Postpartum, Leia was given to Senator [[Bail Prestor Organa|Bail Organa]], and Obi-Wan offered to hand Luke over to the [[Lars family]]. Yoda spoke to Obi-Wan with Qui-Gon, informing him Jinn would also teach him how to retain consciousness after death.<ref name="Episode III" />

During the [[Galactic Civil War]], Polis Massa served as an [[Alliance to Restore the Republic]] regional headquarters and operations sector. Polis Massa was included in a map of [[the galaxy]] that listed [[safe world]]s, [[starfighter]] hubs at level five or higher, regional headquarters and operations sectors, and deep-space caches.<ref name="Rebel Files" />

Vader visited seeking vengeance on those who hid his son from him. After [[Battle at Padmé's tomb|capturing]] [[Tomb of Padmé Amidala|Amidala's tomb]] on [[Naboo]], Vader traveled to Polis Massa with his [[death trooper]]s and [[forensics droid]] [[ZED-6-7]], searching for answers. Arriving at the ruins of the [[Polis Massa Base]], ZED-6-7 said that Polis Massa had been a rebel base prior to being [[Bombardment on Polis Massa|bombarded]] by the [[Galactic Empire|Empire]] years earlier. The [[Amidalans]] who wanted to kill him, believing he was responsible for the deaths of Amidala and Skywalker, followed him there. Vader [[Battle on Polis Massa|deflected]] the blasts from their [[Starship|ships]] and his death [[trooper]]s took control of the [[cannon]]s and destroyed many of their ships. The Amidalans made an attempt at a ground assault, only to be cut down by Vader and his death troopers. When ZED-6-7 found a damaged [[Chroon-Tan B-Machine]] [[Midwife droid|midwifery droid]], he accessed her memory and found footage from the day Amidala had been brought there. Vader then watched the recording of Amidala's final words saying there was still good in Anakin. This infuriated Vader and he cut down the [[droid]] and returned to [[Coruscant]].<ref name="Darth Vader 5">[[Darth Vader (2020) 5|''Darth Vader'' (2020) 5]]</ref>

{{Planet-stub}}

==Behind the scenes==
Created for the [[2005]] film [[Star Wars: Episode III Revenge of the Sith|''Star Wars'': Episode III ''Revenge of the Sith'']],<ref name="Episode III" /> Polis Massa was originally known as Polis Matza during script development of ''Revenge of the Sith''. Slowed-down footage of the [[Hoth asteroid field|asteroid field]] from [[Star Wars: Episode V The Empire Strikes Back|''Star Wars'': Episode V ''The Empire Strikes Back'']] was used as a placeholder for Polis Massa in the evolving edit of Episode III.<ref name="Polis Massa Bts">{{DB|location|polismassa|Polis Massa}}</ref> In the DVD commentary for ''Revenge of the Sith'', [[John Knoll]] explained that [[George Lucas]] designed the look of Polis Massa to be an homage to the look of the [[w:c:2001:Clavius Base|Clavius moon base]] in the [[1960s#1968|1968]] film [[Wikipedia:2001: A Space Odyssey|''2001: A Space Odyssey'']].<ref name="Commentary">{{Film|III}} DVD {{C|Audio Commentary}}</ref>

''[[The Star Wars Book]]'' stated that [[Ordo Eris]] was built on a piece of Polis Massa;<ref name="Star Wars Book">''[[The Star Wars Book]]''</ref> however, the [[2025]] "[[Star Systems of the Galaxy]]" appendix later overrode this and moved it to the [[Chorlian sector]] on the other side of [[the galaxy]].<ref name="Appendix">{{GalaxyMapAppendix}} &mdash; Based on corresponding data for the [[Ordo Eris system]]</ref>

